comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T15:14:51.889Z",codex-gpt5-root,"PR #573 CI evidence: static quality, package boundary, and all token-budget measurements passed, but final rmSync of /tmp/pm-token-budget-AclN4M hit transient ENOTEMPTY. The same gate passed locally before and after the run; this confirms the existing broader temp-lifecycle chore still owns cleanup retry/signal hardening. No script implementation was added in this review slice because the next PR head naturally reruns the full gate and this item's acceptance criteria also require compile-cache plus every mkdtemp caller, not a one-line partial close."
  "2026-07-21T06:54:35.054Z",codex-root-20260721,"Live GitHub evidence 2026-07-21: Auto Release run 29804774154 / GH-626 failed after all coverage measurements when scripts/release/token-budget-gate.mjs final rmSync hit ENOTEMPTY on /tmp/pm-token-budget-fyfySy under Node 24. Reusing this canonical temp-lifecycle item; no duplicate created."
  "2026-07-21T07:33:06.446Z",codex-root-20260721,"Progress evidence: fixed Auto Release GH-626 by routing token-budget cleanup through the shared resilient retry primitive; consolidated external-package and contracts cleanup; added version-scoped compile-cache generation pruning. Broader every-mkdtemp signal cleanup remains, so this item stays open and is released after this PR slice."
  "2026-07-21T07:39:45.232Z",codex-root-20260721,"Verification evidence: both linked cleanup runs now pass (15 token-budget cleanup tests; 26 compile-cache/shared-cleanup tests across four suites)."
  "2026-07-21T07:45:23.196Z",codex-root-20260721,"Full-suite correction: removed the unnecessary existsSync postcondition from cleanupTempRoot so force-recursive deletion remains compatible with partial fs mocks while retaining outer retry/sweep behavior; synthesized non-Error failures now preserve the original value. All 37 cleanup/script tests pass."
  "2026-07-21T07:54:57.149Z",codex-root-20260721,"Final verification: the public compile-cache generation resolver is directly covered alongside pruning and resilient cleanup; the complete 6045-test coverage suite passes at exactly 100% lines/statements/functions/branches. This PR intentionally leaves the broader every-mkdtemp signal-handler acceptance work open."
  "2026-07-21T08:12:07.571Z",codex-root-20260721,"Greptile remediation: compile-cache pruning now reads string directory entries directly instead of allocating Dirent objects only to discard their type metadata. Focused lifecycle coverage remains green."
  "2026-07-21T08:16:41.647Z",codex-root-20260721,"Final review-head proof: the allocation simplification and resilient cleanup path pass the complete 6052-test suite at exact 100% coverage."
  "2026-07-21T09:10:30.997Z",codex-root-20260721,"Hosted review remediation: compile-cache generation names now reject unsafe filename tokens and pruning retains a bounded fresh-concurrency grace so two pm versions starting together cannot delete one another. A real filesystem race test removes a candidate between readdir and stat; only ENOENT is ignored and all other failures remain visible."
  "2026-07-21T09:15:16.813Z",codex-root-20260721,"Exact remediation-head proof: all 332 test files and 6053 tests pass at 100/100/100/100 coverage. This PR completes bounded, concurrency-safe compile-cache generations and resilient cleanup surfaces, while the remaining every-mkdtemp signal-handler work stays open in this same canonical item."
  "2026-07-21T10:13:36.637Z",codex-root-20260721,"Hosted CI remediation: Windows Node 24 exhausted the prior 375 ms helper retry window with EBUSY on the generated workspace. Test sandboxes now apply Node's recursive rm retry contract plus the same eight-attempt 120 ms backoff used by production cleanup."
  "2026-07-21T10:14:17.179Z",codex-root-20260721,"Hosted CodeRabbit remediation: compile-cache validation now accepts leading underscore and hyphen safe tokens, matching resolveCompileCacheGeneration for scoped package names such as @org/package while continuing to reject dot segments and path separators. Focused SDK and scale-workspace suites pass (10 tests)."
  "2026-07-21T10:29:28.119Z",codex-root-20260721,"Exact final-head proof: 332 test files and 6053 tests pass; compile-cache scoped-package generation and Windows-portable cleanup are covered within 100% statements (40688/40688), branches (28623/28623), functions (8264/8264), and lines (39582/39582)."
  "2026-07-21T10:31:05.390Z",codex-root-20260721,"Installed-package acceptance proof: pnpm smoke:npx packed the current tree, installed it into a fresh temporary project, exercised the CLI and all 13 bundled packages, and cleaned the sandbox successfully (version 2026.7.21)."
  "2026-07-21T10:47:25.985Z",codex-root-20260721,"Final exact-commit Greptile review scored 5/5 with no comments, but noted a soft resolver/validator contract gap for empty or leading-dot inputs. Tightening the public resolver invariant before push."
  "2026-07-21T10:52:29.795Z",codex-root-20260721,"Greptile contract remediation verified: resolver now trims empty versions to development and rewrites a leading dot, so every generated token is accepted by pruning; scoped, empty, dot-prefixed, and traversal-shaped cases are covered. Full 6053-test suite remains exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-07-22T19:18:04.059Z",codex-sdk-boundary-20260722,"GitHub provenance: GH-626 now contains a direct system-of-record link to this canonical release temp/cache cleanup lineage; the GitHub issue is closed while this broader pm follow-up remains open."
  "2026-08-09T16:21:33.779Z","harness:codex","Fresh reproduction 2026-08-09 after PR #952: the published 2026.8.9 installed-agent verifier completed all 10 lifecycle steps under both npm and Bun with ok:true, then the verifier process exited nonzero because final recursive cleanup hit ENOTEMPTY on its temporary root. Reusing this broader open item rather than creating a duplicate; the result proves acceptance behavior is healthy while cleanup can still mask success."
  "2026-09-18T23:35:36.587Z","harness:codex","Current-tranche reproduction: the default temporary filesystem user quota refused writes during npm tarball extraction and interrupted broad coverage setup. An external scratch root with no initialized tracker in its ancestors restores isolation; a home-relative external root still discovers the home tracker in tests that intentionally unset PM_PATH, as already documented in the Sep 8 note. No unrelated temporary artifacts were deleted. This remains the canonical footprint/cleanup follow-up; no duplicate created."
  "2026-09-21T09:55:08.917Z","harness:codex","Current implementation scope: shared process-owned sandbox lifecycle and adoption by package smoke, dogfood, contract snapshot, plugin MCP harness and sandboxed test runner. Existing compile-cache generation pruning remains in place. Signal cleanup must stop registered children before deleting their workspace, preserve explicit keep-temp requests, and unregister normal-completion resources. SIGKILL cannot run cleanup; do not claim that guarantee."
  "2026-09-21T10:06:14.090Z","harness:codex","Verification: 86 focused tests passed across lease ownership, cleanup, package smoke, contract snapshots and plugin MCP harness. Both new or changed lifecycle primitives separately meet exact 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines (73 statements, 40 branches, 9 functions, 67 lines). Real subprocess tests prove normal exit, uncaught failure, explicit retention and Unix interrupts. Adoption currently covers five primary smoke and contract entrypoints; test-runner and other release/benchmark scripts remain pending under this broader canonical item."
  "2026-09-21T10:14:51.540Z","harness:codex","Full-suite attempt: 9167 tests passed and three existing scale/refusal tests timed out under concurrent local validation load; no valid full coverage report was produced. Preserving all thresholds and timeout contracts; rerun with reduced worker concurrency after other gates finish. Packed npm/npx/bunx smoke and package-first dogfood passed; published 2026.9.21 npm/Bun installed-agent lifecycle and npx/bunx MCP stdio/HTTP verification also passed."
  "2026-09-21T10:23:21.468Z","harness:codex","Final changed-script coverage: 132 tests across seven suites passed at exact 786/786 statements, 392/392 branches, 113/113 functions and 761/761 lines. Both plugin MCP smoke workflows passed. An independent temporary-directory manual run exercised CLI init/create/claim/update/comments/notes/learnings/close/release/validate and confirmed complete closed-state reads through the public PmClient SDK. Linked test executions are recorded by pm test; remaining runner migration remains explicitly open."
  "2026-09-21T10:42:39.361Z","harness:codex","PR 1283 review: accepting CodeRabbit finding 4061327789. Exit-time console output can be buffered on piped stderr, so retained-workspace diagnostics will use best-effort synchronous writes while preserving the original failure if stderr is unavailable. Add observable output and closed-stderr regressions. First hosted round settled with 37 successful, one neutral and two skipped checks; Sourcery reported review quota exhaustion."
  "2026-09-21T10:50:33.971Z","harness:codex","Completed five-entrypoint delivery is now represented by child pm-14dnbh so package-generated release notes include the shipped behavior. This parent remains open and unclaimed for the explicitly inventoried runner, benchmark and release-script migration."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T06:09:36.684Z","harness:codex","Temporary storage observation 2026-09-08: the host default temporary filesystem reached its 1,048,576-inode limit while still showing free bytes. Tests honoring an external tmpdir could proceed, but hard-coded /tmp fixtures still failed. The current isolation repair pm-bukwmy switches the affected vector, SDK exemplar and MCP Skills fixtures to owned tmpdir roots and preserves cleanup. No unrelated temporary files were deleted. A scratch directory beneath another initialized tracker can still affect ancestor-discovery tests even when outside this checkout; document that boundary and keep long-term temporary footprint/cleanup and runner isolation as separate acceptance scopes."
  "2026-09-21T10:17:53.904Z","harness:codex","Remaining lifecycle adoption inventory after this delivery: scripts/run-tests.mjs; bench/point-read-costs, context-read-costs, run-scale-benchmarks and cli-transport-floor; release/verify-published-release, verify-installed-agent-session, docs-skills-gate, packed-first-run, context-eval-gate, isolated-regression-control, run-release-pipeline, agent-task-token-gate, refusal-closure-gate, token-budget-gate, context-intent-calibration-gate and compatibility-check (all .mjs under scripts). Review each full producer/consumer lifecycle before registration; async children require bounded stop-before-delete callbacks. Existing finally cleanup is not proof of interrupt cleanup. SIGKILL, power loss and forced Windows process termination cannot execute process cleanup handlers."
